# PVC Documentation Rules (English Canonical)

> Korean siblings: `docs/codemap-maintenance.mdc`, `documentation-standard.mdc`, `reference-catalog.mdc`.

## 1. CODEMAP

- Keep root `CODEMAP.md` (or equivalent) with: purpose/users, stack/runbook, top folders/files, screen/API/DB/vendor links, entry points/data flows, build/test/deploy/backup, secret *locations* (not values), dependency/version cautions, known limits/debt.
- Any new/changed/removed folder, feature, API, model, env var, or integration updates CODEMAP before “done”.
- CODEMAP ≠ code ⇒ not done.

## 2. Documentation Standard

- Document structural, schema, integration, design-token, and security-policy changes (purpose, targets, blast radius, migration/recovery, verification, rollback, follow-ups).
- Single source of truth per concern: README, CODEMAP, ARCHITECTURE, DESIGN, TYPEGUIDE, CHANGELOG, `.cursor/rules/`, `docs/`, and `docs/references/SOURCES.md` + `GITHUB_STAR_CATALOG.md`.

## 3. External Catalogs

- High-star GitHub proposals: `docs/references/GITHUB_STAR_CATALOG.md`
- Official standards provenance: `docs/references/SOURCES.md`
- Import flow always through `core/03` + English `en/core.mdc` §4.
